silm:instances_papers_11_base_commutative_diagram_chapters_05_relator_quotient_projection_sections_01_relator_to_congruence_closure_concrete_anchor_22_CheeseTrapFace#cheesetrapface silm:hasLongDescription "The CheeseTrapFace is the rejected sentence pattern where unrestricted prose enters in olog position. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'CheeseTrapFace', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
